summary:
  The relayed-Ogg reader gives up at the first place a field name stands
  without a sane length in front of it.

history:
  The reader took the last place the letters TITLE= or ARTIST= stood and
  returned nothing when the four bytes ahead were no field length. But
  ALBUMARTIST= ends in ARTIST= and SUBTITLE= in TITLE=: a block that names
  the album's artist after the track's lost its artist, and one with a
  subtitle lost the title too. Found 2026-11-10 with built comment blocks.
  The search now goes on with what stands before such a place.

target:
  package/contents/ui/reader.py

find:
              end = pos + len(key) - 1

replace:
              return -1, ""

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_reader_oggbuf.py::test_a_longer_name_ending_in_the_same_letters_is_another_field
  and tests/test_reader_oggbuf.py::test_a_block_cut_off_mid_title_leaves_the_last_whole_one.
  Line-neutral.
